═══ R8 EN reply complete (collagen/vegetarian) — guard: clean ═══
Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Thank you for asking before taking it — that care itself shows how seriously you've kept your vow these 14 years. 🙏

**What Master Lu taught about this**

Master Lu was asked directly about supplements containing animal by-products. His answer:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

— *Answered: Frequently Asked Questions About Practising Buddhism*

Ordinary collagen is made from animal skin, bone, or fish — so it falls into this same category. Master Lu's guidance is: **best to avoid it if there is another way.**

But he also never asked us to damage our bodies for the sake of a vow:

> We should ensure that we have a balanced diet, as we need to take care of our bodies. Buddhas and Bodhisattvas would also like us to have a healthy body so that we can practise Buddhism better.

**So, practically**

1. **Go back to your doctor first** and ask specifically: *is there a vegetarian/plant-based option for my condition?* For bones, doctors often work with calcium, vitamin D3, vitamin K2, soy protein, and vitamin C (which the body uses to build its own collagen). Many of these are fully vegetarian. Ask before assuming animal collagen is the only path.

2. **If your doctor says there is genuinely no vegetarian alternative** and your bones are at real risk, Master Lu taught that in situations of no choice, you say in your heart before taking it:

   *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva forgive me, [your full name]. I am taking this only because I have no choice for my health. I do not wish to consume it at all."*

   The key, as Master Lu said, is your intention — you are not taking it out of craving.

3. **Don't stop your medical treatment.** Master Lu's way is body and mind together — medicine treats the physical, Buddhism clears the karmic side. Both hands.

**Recitations to support your bones**

- 📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 7 times daily
  *"Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, please bless and protect me, [full name], with good health and heal my spine and bones."*

- 📿 **Heart Sutra** — 7 times daily (not after 10pm)
  *"...please bless me, [full name], with wisdom, a clear and calm mind."*

- 📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** — start from 1 time daily
  *"...please help me, [full name], repent and eliminate the karmic obstacles causing the illness in my spine and bones."*

Keep going steadily. Don't watch for results — do the practice and leave the timing to Bodhisattva. 🙏

May I ask — are you already doing a daily recitation, or would this be a new start for you? That way I can suggest the right next step.

