  ✓ AND asks the triage question in the same reply
  ✓ no generic 「I dedicate all merits」 closing
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
That's a good question to ask 🙏

Before I suggest where to start, let me understand your situation a little:

**Have you chanted before, or is this completely new to you?**

This matters because Master Lu's approach is staged — beginners start with just two sutras and build up slowly. Sincere consistency matters far more than volume.

If you tell me you're brand new, here's roughly where we'd begin:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say:
> "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health, safety and good fortune."

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say:
> "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom."

(Best not to recite the Heart Sutra after 10PM, or during thunderstorms.)

Also remember to recite the **full title** of each sutra before you begin the text itself.

If you can't read the Chinese yet, that's completely fine — there are chant-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Just follow along. Nobody starts off fluent.

Once you've built up a steady rhythm, we can talk about adding the Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance and other mantras suited to your specific situation.

So — have you chanted before? 🙏

