  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
I'm sorry you're going through this — not sleeping wears a person down completely. 🙏

Before I suggest anything specific, let me ask one thing: **have you recited before, or is this completely new to you?**

That changes what I'd recommend as a starting point.

But I can tell you what Master Lu teaches for a restless, unsettled mind — the Heart Sutra is the key one. Master Lu's guidance on the Heart Sutra is:

> "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, \<your full name\>, grant me wisdom."

The Heart Sutra opens wisdom and clears away worry and mental agitation — which is usually what keeps us awake.

**If you're starting fresh, begin simply:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times daily
Prayer before reciting: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health, safety and good fortune."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times daily
Prayer before reciting: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and free me from worries."*

⚠️ **Important timing note:** Do not recite the Heart Sutra after 10pm, or during heavy rain, thunderstorms, or lightning. Recite it during the daytime — especially since you're already physically weakened by lack of sleep.

If you don't know the texts yet, there are follow-along recitation videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

**One honest thing:** Heart Dharma Door teaches caring for both body and mind together. Severe insomnia can have medical causes too — please also see a doctor. Recitation clears the obstacles on the spiritual side; the physical side needs proper medical care. **Both hands working together — that's how it heals fastest.**

Keep reciting steadily. Don't recite waiting to see if it "works" — just do the practice and let Bodhisattva arrange the rest. 🙏

So — have you recited before, or is this your first time?

