--- reply ---
Arguing at home is really draining — I understand 🙏

Let me ask one thing first so I give you the right starting point: **have you chanted before, or is this completely new to you?**

In the meantime, here's a simple way to begin. Start small and keep it steady:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times a day (build up to 7 once you're comfortable)
Before you begin, say:
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and a calm mind."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times a day (build up to 7)
Before you begin, say:
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove my worries."*
(Not after 10pm)

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 to 49 times a day, for the family member you argue with most
Before you begin, say:
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [their full name], to transform and resolve our negative karmic ties."*

If you don't know how to pronounce the words, don't worry — there are follow-along chanting videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Master Lu explained why this friction happens:

> If a child is always having conflicts with their parents or family members, it may be due to negative karmic ties from previous lives or the child may have come into the parents' lives to collect karmic debts. The recitation of the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots (Chieh Chieh Chou) is also required.

— *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3, Q127*

The same principle applies between spouses, siblings, in-laws — anyone in the family. So we don't fight the person; we work on dissolving what's underneath.

One practical note: it's usually better not to tell the family member you're reciting for them. Just do it quietly and let your own temper soften first — that's what changes the atmosphere at home.

Keep chanting consistently, and Guan Yin Bodhisattva will help at the right time 🙏

Let me know if you've chanted before, and I'll adjust this for you.

