Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
This is one of the hardest parts of being a parent 🙏 The worry and frustration wear you down more than anything the child actually does.

Master Lu was very direct about the first thing parents need to check — themselves. In *Buddhism Q&A* he said:

> First, you should not use an adult's way of thinking to restrain the innocent and playful nature of children.

And there's one more thing he warned parents about, which many people don't know. From *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3*:

> If a child is very stubborn, hard to discipline, or display unruly behaviours, then it would be best that you limit your recitation of the Great Compassion Mantra to 7 times per day. If you recite a large number of the Great Compassion Mantra for misbehaved children, it may increase their spiritual power and therefore it would be even more difficult for you to discipline them.

So for a rebellious child, the medicine is **not** more energy — it's **wisdom** and **untying the knot** between you two.

**For your own emotions:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 to 7 times daily
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and increased spiritual strength."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 to 7 times daily
Say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and be free from worries."*
(Not after 10pm)

**For the relationship with your child:**

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 to 49 times daily
Say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and my child [child's full name], to resolve our negative karmic ties."*

📿 **Heart Sutra for your child** — you can recite separately for them, asking Guan Yin Bodhisattva to grant [child's full name] wisdom and help them listen to their parents.

One caution Master Lu gave: don't recite the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots excessively, and don't try to forcefully change your child's own causality. Soften the knot — don't pull on it.

Keep going with this. Don't watch for signs — watch your own consistency. The change usually shows up in *your* patience first, and the child responds to that.

If you're not sure how to recite the scriptures, there are follow-along videos here: 🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Have you been reciting before, or is this new to you? 🙏

*Reference: Buddhism Q&A (Q114, Q127), Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3*

