Q: My family member is ill, what should I recite for them?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
I'm sorry to hear about your family member 🙏 You can definitely recite for them — the important thing is that you say their **full name** in your prayer, otherwise the recitation doesn't reach them.

Here's where to start:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou)** — 3 to 7 times a day
Before reciting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless [family member's full name], grant them good health, and cure the illness in [part of the body]."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Hsin Ching)** — 3 to 7 times a day
Before reciting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless [family member's full name], grant them wisdom."*
(Please don't recite the Heart Sutra after 10pm, or during thunderstorms.)

📿 **Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance (Li Fo Ta Chan Hui Wen)** — start with 1 time a day
Before reciting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], help me repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."*
(Start at 1 — this one activates karma, so don't push it higher at the beginning. Also not after 10pm.)

A couple of important notes from Master Lu's teachings:

- If your family member is **seriously ill and physically weak**, they should recite mainly the Great Compassion Mantra themselves, and **avoid** the Heart Sutra and the Amitabha Pure Land Rebirth Mantra.
- If they're in hospital, recite the Great Compassion Mantra as much as you can for your own protection too.
- Buddhism here **supports** medical treatment, it doesn't replace it. Please keep following the doctors — recitation works alongside proper medical care.

If you're not sure how to pronounce the sutras, there are chanting videos you can follow along with:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Keep going steadily — don't set a deadline in your mind for when things should improve. Faith, vow, action: believe first, then practise. Bodhisattva will help at the right time 🙏

Can I ask — **have you recited before, or is this completely new to you?** And roughly how serious is your family member's condition? That will help me point you to the right next step.

